# Width overrides

Most sections and cards choose a sensible width themselves. Change a width only when the layout needs it, such as a graph that is hard to read at half width.

These settings work in the Sections view only. A Masonry or Panel view ignores them.

## Make a section wider

Set **Width** in the section settings, or `column_span` in YAML. A section is 1 column wide by default. It can span up to the number of sections set for the view.

To make the Energy section span 2 columns on a tablet or wall panel, set its width in the section settings. On a phone it still takes the full width.

```yaml
type: grid
column_span: 2
cards:
  - type: heading
    heading: Energy today
  - type: energy-usage-graph
```

A wider section has a wider grid: 12 columns for each column it spans. In a section 2 columns wide, a card set to 12 columns fills half of it. Use `full` to fill the whole width at any span.

## Change a card's size

Open the card's **Layout** tab, or set `grid_options` in YAML.

| Option | What it sets | Values |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `columns` | How many grid columns the card takes | A number, or `full` |
| `rows` | How many 56px rows the card takes | A number, or `auto` to fit the content |

This YAML sets 3 room temperatures in a row, each a third of a section wide. Each card keeps `rows: auto`, so it grows if a room name wraps.

```yaml
- type: tile
  entity: sensor.kitchen_temperature
  name: Kitchen
  grid_options:
    columns: 4
    rows: auto
```

Do not give a card with text a fixed height. A long room name or a translated label must be able to wrap.
